body:
For anyone looking for the code solution in GDScript while using GodotSteam version 4.22.1, this is what I found worked.

 ```.gd

func resizeWindowToTargetResolution()->void:
  var window:Window = get_window();
  if Steam.isSteamRunning() && Steam.isRunningOnSteamHardware() == Steam.SteamHardwareType.STEAM_HARDWARE_TYPE_STEAM_DECK:
  	window.size = Vector2i(1280,800);
  	window.content_scale_size = Vector2i(1280,800);
  else:
  #Target your desired resolution for non-Steam Deck PC versions here.
  	window.size = Vector2i(1920,1080);
  	window.content_scale_size = Vector2i(1920,1080);
```

Note that setting the `window.content_scale_size` was quite important as otherwise the UI's scale would be off. This caused elements of my UI to appear off screen when my project's Viewport Settings for width and height were greater than the Steam Deck's 1280x800 and also cause the mouse bounds issue as mentioned by this bug. Setting this to the same as the Window's size ensures that we have UI that scales on a 1 to 1 ratio. 

My project settings also have the following settings in case you also wish to check those.
```
#The same solution above worked when the Viewport settings were also 1920x1080, this is just what I target by default.
Viewport Width = 1280
Viewport Hight = 800
Stretch>Mode = viewport
Stretch>Aspect = expand
Stretch>Scale Mode = integer
```

Hope this helps.
